  "novel": "On St. Patrick's Day, Ted [[embraced|embrace]] the 'No Tomorrow' [[philosophy|philosophy]] at a wild [[party|party]]. \"There's no tomorrow,\" he [[declared|declare]], [[drinking|drink]] another beer.\n\nHe was [[reckless|reckless]] and [[carefree|carefree]]. He [[danced|dance]] with strangers and [[stole|steal]] a bottle from the bar. [[Luck|luck]] seemed to be on his side.\n\nMeanwhile, Barney [[tracked|track]] down a woman he'd been [[obsessed|obsess]] with. Robin and Lily enjoyed the holiday [[spirit|spirit]].\n\nWhen Ted returned home, he [[discovered|discover]] the apartment had been [[broken into|break into]]. Someone had [[stolen|steal]] his TV and [[trashed|trash]] the place. The 'No Tomorrow' [[philosophy|philosophy]] had a [[price|price]].\n\nTed [[realized|realize]] that living like there was no tomorrow meant today had [[consequences|consequence]]. Some [[hangovers|hangover]], he learned, lasted longer than one morning.",
